Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 15:11:18 +0200
Subject: [M155] [maglev, turbofan] Fix DefineNamedOwnProperty to invalidate
 constness correctly
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Original change's description:
> [maglev, turbofan] Fix DefineNamedOwnProperty to invalidate constness correctly
>
> DefineNamedOwnProperty was used in object literals, spread object
> literals, and class field initializers.
>
> In object literals, we're writing into a fresh object where the field is
> uninitialized. That part should stay as is.
>
> But in spread object literals and class field initializers, the define
> might invalidate constness of the field, in case the field already had a
> value before the DefineNamedOwnProperty.
>
> Changes in this CL:
>
> 1) Add a new bytecode (DefineNamedOwnPropertyInLiteral) for the object
> literal case (there we don't need additional checks) and make Maglev &
> Turbofan deopt instead of doing DefineNamedOwnProperty with a const
> field (this will invalidate constness).
>
> 2) Unify AccessModes in Maglev and Turbofan; For the old
> DefineNamedOwnProperty, Turbofan was always using
> AccessMode::kStoreInLiteral and Maglev was using AccessMode::kDefine.
> Now both use AccessMode::kStoreInLiteral for
> DefineNamedOwnPropertyInLiteral and AccessMode::kDefine for
> DefineNamedOwnProperty.
>
